1
00:01:34,465 --> 00:01:36,968
Look at the vulgar filth printed here.

2
00:01:37,168 --> 00:01:38,769
-Please do something. -I see.

3
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:42,774
-Our taxes pay your salary, you know. -Yes, I'll get on it. Sorry.

4
00:01:42,974 --> 00:01:44,208
I'll call you later.

5
00:01:44,442 --> 00:01:46,511
Doesn't anybody think of the children?

6
00:01:46,744 --> 00:01:48,513
I'm hungry!

7
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:50,515
Are you even listening?

8
00:01:50,748 --> 00:01:52,517
Excuse me! I'm looking for...

9
00:01:59,056 --> 00:02:00,191
Shut up!

10
00:02:04,529 --> 00:02:07,665
People are trying to work, and you're being a nuisance.

11
00:02:08,166 --> 00:02:10,168
Sorry. It slipped out of my hand.

12
00:02:10,368 --> 00:02:14,772
Can't you even make a cup of tea? This is why you'll never land a man.

13
00:02:15,306 --> 00:02:16,307
Look around you.

14
00:02:16,507 --> 00:02:21,212
Hiromi-san, Keiko-san, and even Kaoru-san all got married.

15
00:02:21,412 --> 00:02:25,183
You'll be the last spinster left before you know it.

16
00:02:25,650 --> 00:02:28,252
Would you butt out? What's it to you, anyway?

17
00:02:28,486 --> 00:02:30,321
Next time get your own tea!

18
00:02:30,521 --> 00:02:32,190
Jeez, you're prickly.

19
00:02:33,090 --> 00:02:35,393
I could land a man, I just don't want to.

20
00:02:38,029 --> 00:02:40,565
And writing apology letters isn't your real job.

21
00:02:40,798 --> 00:02:42,733
What? Why you...!

22
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:43,568
Huh?

23
00:02:44,268 --> 00:02:45,903
Why is everyone so damn noisy?

24
00:02:50,675 --> 00:02:51,742
What's going on?

25
00:03:05,256 --> 00:03:07,091
What the heck? Who is that?

26
00:03:07,291 --> 00:03:08,426
Please, don't be...

27
00:03:18,402 --> 00:03:20,037
Reiko-chan!

28
00:03:21,239 --> 00:03:22,273
I knew it.

29
00:03:22,773 --> 00:03:23,774
Yes!

30
00:03:24,308 --> 00:03:27,545
Yes, yes, yes!

31
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:30,715
Are you all right, sir?

32
00:03:30,915 --> 00:03:33,217
Ouch. That was a hard impact.

33
00:03:33,784 --> 00:03:35,386
Jeez, Dad.

34
00:03:35,586 --> 00:03:37,255
Dad? No way!

35
00:03:37,455 --> 00:03:39,123
Yep. That's Reiko's dad.

36
00:03:39,323 --> 00:03:42,159
Can't believe that guy's some big corporate president.

37
00:03:43,394 --> 00:03:44,629
Are you okay, Dad?

38
00:03:44,862 --> 00:03:46,697
Oh... Reiko!

39
00:03:47,865 --> 00:03:49,133
What's with the drop in?

40
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:53,404
You never answer the phone, so I stopped by on my business trip.

41
00:03:54,872 --> 00:03:56,908
What a messy police station.

42
00:03:57,108 --> 00:03:59,910
Who could work in a dump like this?

43
00:04:00,111 --> 00:04:02,480
You're the one who made it so messy!

44
00:04:03,114 --> 00:04:07,251
If I were in charge, I'd tear this place down and build a wonderful new office.

45
00:04:07,451 --> 00:04:11,322
If we ever get privatized, go ahead and buy the station from us.

46
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:15,092
Is this Reiko's desk?

47
00:04:15,293 --> 00:04:16,060
Yes.

48
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:18,629
So cheap! This won't do at all.

49
00:04:18,829 --> 00:04:21,098
How can you stand it?

50
00:04:21,299 --> 00:04:22,733
The chair's awful too.

51
00:04:23,301 --> 00:04:25,836
Oh! What a shabby kitchen!

52
00:04:26,137 --> 00:04:28,839
Ew! What an unsanitary toilet!

53
00:04:29,473 --> 00:04:31,976
This is no place for a human to work.

54
00:04:32,176 --> 00:04:35,513
I never realized Reiko was being treated so badly.

55
00:04:35,746 --> 00:04:38,849
Did you come all the way from Kobe just to complain?

56
00:04:39,350 --> 00:04:40,084
That does it!

57
00:04:40,751 --> 00:04:42,019
You there. Takeshita!

58
00:04:42,219 --> 00:04:43,120
Yes, sir!

59
00:04:43,321 --> 00:04:45,356
Commence Operation 189!

60
00:04:48,492 --> 00:04:49,860
What's going on? Hey!

61
00:04:50,394 --> 00:04:52,196
-Step outside. -Hey, stop that!

62
00:04:52,930 --> 00:04:53,964
-Hey! -Wait, Dad!

63
00:04:54,398 --> 00:04:58,002
Daddy's got things all under control, so you go patrol or something.

64
00:04:58,336 --> 00:05:02,707
Hey, Dad? Open the door. Hey, open the door!

65
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:04,041
Jeez, Dad!

66
00:05:04,241 --> 00:05:07,011
Your dad's a weirdo, Reiko.

67
00:05:11,482 --> 00:05:12,216
Oh!

68
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:14,418
What is that?

69
00:05:15,586 --> 00:05:19,724
Ryotsu! Why is there a helicopter here? This is your doing again, isn't it?

70
00:05:19,957 --> 00:05:21,592
No, not this time!

71
00:05:21,826 --> 00:05:23,361
Actually, Chief...

72
00:05:23,561 --> 00:05:24,428
Huh?

73
00:05:25,363 --> 00:05:26,430
Thanks for waiting.

74
00:05:28,799 --> 00:05:29,999
Oh!

75
00:05:34,171 --> 00:05:36,607
This is the latest in office automation.

76
00:05:36,841 --> 00:05:39,276
So lavish. Hard to believe it's the station.

77
00:05:40,010 --> 00:05:41,912
This desk is the same as before.

78
00:05:42,246 --> 00:05:44,181
Here is a modern heated toilet seat.

79
00:05:44,382 --> 00:05:45,383
Oh yeah?

80
00:05:45,583 --> 00:05:46,917
It's definitely warm.

81
00:05:47,151 --> 00:05:50,087
This kitchen system is made in West Germany.

82
00:05:50,755 --> 00:05:51,922
Well, Reiko?

83
00:05:52,456 --> 00:05:54,158
What on earth is going on here?

84
00:05:54,358 --> 00:05:58,763
Thanks for looking after my daughter. I'm Reiko's father, Pyunpyunmaru Akimoto.

85
00:05:58,996 --> 00:06:00,698
Oh, nice to meet you.

86
00:06:01,532 --> 00:06:03,467
Wow, look at that flame.

87
00:06:03,701 --> 00:06:04,468
Nice.

88
00:06:04,702 --> 00:06:08,038
This baby will boil water for instant ramen in no time.

89
00:06:08,239 --> 00:06:09,106
Ryo-san...

90
00:06:09,306 --> 00:06:12,610
Well, Reiko? Do you like it? So much nicer for you to work in.

91
00:06:12,843 --> 00:06:15,112
Ugh, just put everything back how it was!

92
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,248
Huh?

93
00:06:18,282 --> 00:06:22,286
After all the trouble I went through, you want me to put it all back?

94
00:06:22,486 --> 00:06:25,322
Yes. And why don't you tell me why you're really here?

95
00:06:25,589 --> 00:06:27,291
Oh, right.

96
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:32,496
Sure is a huge stack of matchmaking photos.

97
00:06:32,730 --> 00:06:36,567
They arrive almost every day from business partners and banks.

98
00:06:36,934 --> 00:06:38,903
Just a little look, sweetie?

99
00:06:39,103 --> 00:06:40,304
There are so many.

100
00:06:40,671 --> 00:06:43,441
It'll take days just to look at them all.

101
00:06:44,241 --> 00:06:46,343
Come on, Reiko. How about this one?

102
00:06:46,577 --> 00:06:49,447
He's the eldest son of the Yasui conglomerate...

103
00:06:49,647 --> 00:06:51,582
Sorry, Dad. Please turn him down.

104
00:06:51,782 --> 00:06:53,684
I don't want to get married yet.

105
00:06:54,251 --> 00:06:54,919
What?

106
00:06:55,586 --> 00:06:56,921
I'm sorry.

107
00:06:58,989 --> 00:07:00,925
Well, all righty then.

108
00:07:01,125 --> 00:07:01,992
Really?

109
00:07:02,326 --> 00:07:05,162
I only brought these photos because they asked me to.

110
00:07:05,896 --> 00:07:07,665
It's your life and your choice.

111
00:07:08,165 --> 00:07:09,633
I believe in you.

112
00:07:09,834 --> 00:07:10,468
Dad.

113
00:07:10,968 --> 00:07:12,470
-Clear these out. -Yes, sir!

114
00:07:12,803 --> 00:07:13,504
I'm glad.

115
00:07:13,704 --> 00:07:16,507
-What a reasonable father. -I guess so.

116
00:07:16,707 --> 00:07:19,443
-But would you look at just one for me? -What?

117
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:22,179
His family owns Ohgane Real Estate.

118
00:07:22,446 --> 00:07:24,982
I have a long-standing relationship with them,

119
00:07:25,182 --> 00:07:27,451
so I can't just reject him out of hand.

120
00:07:27,952 --> 00:07:30,187
-Would you at least meet him? -But...

121
00:07:30,387 --> 00:07:32,623
Sir, it's time for your meeting.

122
00:07:32,823 --> 00:07:33,691
Oh, right.

123
00:07:33,924 --> 00:07:34,992
Wait, Dad.

124
00:07:35,392 --> 00:07:37,528
Thanks, Reiko!

125
00:07:38,362 --> 00:07:40,464
Jeez, Dad...

126
00:07:40,664 --> 00:07:45,402
The only son of Ohgane Real Estate, 32 years old, 2,000 tsubo house in Ashiya.

127
00:07:45,636 --> 00:07:48,172
Hmph, looks like a shriveled cucumber.

128
00:07:48,839 --> 00:07:51,742
A top company with an annual turnover of 70 billion yen.

129
00:07:51,976 --> 00:07:55,212
Guess it can't be helped. I'll meet him and turn him down.

130
00:07:55,412 --> 00:07:59,049
You're going to turn him down? What a waste. That's 70 billion yen!

131
00:07:59,283 --> 00:08:00,851
It's not about the money.

132
00:08:01,285 --> 00:08:03,754
What if you meet him and he really likes you?

133
00:08:03,988 --> 00:08:06,524
It'll be even more awkward to turn him down.

134
00:08:06,824 --> 00:08:10,127
That's true. It could look even more rude.

135
00:08:10,361 --> 00:08:13,397
Really? So what should I do? This is a problem.

136
00:08:13,597 --> 00:08:15,166
Don't you worry.

137
00:08:15,366 --> 00:08:17,368
Just act like you always do.

138
00:08:17,568 --> 00:08:20,905
You'll scare him off and he'll turn you down instead.

139
00:08:21,138 --> 00:08:22,907
What do you mean by that?

140
00:08:24,708 --> 00:08:27,912
"Stop messing around, or I'll knock you out, Ryo-chan."

141
00:08:28,612 --> 00:08:31,048
"I'm Reiko from Kameari Park Police Station."

142
00:08:31,248 --> 00:08:33,551
"Don't make me throw you in the river."

143
00:08:34,018 --> 00:08:35,553
Cut it out, Ryo-chan!

144
00:08:35,753 --> 00:08:38,022
"Cut it out, Ryo-chan!"

145
00:08:38,455 --> 00:08:40,424
When have I ever done that?

146
00:08:41,592 --> 00:08:43,627
-There it is! -What?

147
00:08:47,565 --> 00:08:49,400
Reiko-san...

148
00:08:54,872 --> 00:08:57,541
The Akimoto family are late.

149
00:08:57,741 --> 00:09:01,378
Yes, you're right. They're now more than an hour late.

150
00:09:02,112 --> 00:09:04,281
Mommy, I have to pee.

151
00:09:04,481 --> 00:09:05,382
Hold it in!

152
00:09:05,583 --> 00:09:07,718
Remember why you're here, Kazuo-san.

153
00:09:07,918 --> 00:09:10,888
You're here to get her to marry you, no matter what.

154
00:09:11,355 --> 00:09:14,725
The Akimotos are a financial powerhouse, far wealthier than us.

155
00:09:14,925 --> 00:09:18,829
Their assets could eventually be yours.

156
00:09:19,597 --> 00:09:24,368
You will turn a blind eye to any flaws! Even if she has a temper.

157
00:09:24,568 --> 00:09:25,836
Okay, Mommy.

158
00:09:26,070 --> 00:09:28,405
Sorry we're late. Hello, hello.

159
00:09:28,606 --> 00:09:29,673
There they are.

160
00:09:30,674 --> 00:09:34,945
I'm Reiko's uncle. Her father has a cold, so I've come in his place.

161
00:09:35,145 --> 00:09:36,046
Huh?

162
00:09:39,049 --> 00:09:41,118
I'm Reiko. Nice to meet you.

163
00:09:50,961 --> 00:09:53,264
She looks completely different, Mommy.

164
00:09:54,331 --> 00:09:56,133
&lt;i&gt;No way he still wants in.&lt;/i&gt;

165
00:09:56,333 --> 00:09:58,769
&lt;i&gt;If I pull this off, I get to eat katsudon.&lt;/i&gt;

166
00:09:59,236 --> 00:10:01,805
So this is Reiko-san?

167
00:10:02,006 --> 00:10:04,642
Yes. Is something the matter?

168
00:10:04,842 --> 00:10:08,512
No, it's just that she looks a little different from her photo.

169
00:10:09,546 --> 00:10:13,317
I get that a lot. I don't photograph well.

170
00:10:14,084 --> 00:10:17,254
Reiko-san, you have a very husky voice.

171
00:10:17,454 --> 00:10:20,157
Yeah, from smoking 500 cigarettes a day.

172
00:10:20,357 --> 00:10:24,628
I also drink loads of shochu and beer, and sing karaoke.

173
00:10:24,828 --> 00:10:29,700
Oh my, what a lot of hobbies... And you also ride horses, don't you?

174
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:32,136
I love horses. Especially horse racing.

175
00:10:32,336 --> 00:10:35,105
I love my racing, mahjong, gambling, and cards.

176
00:10:35,305 --> 00:10:37,908
And karate, and boxing, and fighting as well.

177
00:10:38,142 --> 00:10:40,344
You can't beat a good brawl.

178
00:10:40,544 --> 00:10:42,746
The more blood, the better!

179
00:10:43,881 --> 00:10:45,716
Reiko-san, you're very funny.

180
00:10:46,350 --> 00:10:51,121
Oh no, I'm being serious. Would you like a little demonstration?

181
00:10:51,321 --> 00:10:52,222
Hey.

182
00:10:52,556 --> 00:10:57,194
Don't go too far. Remember Reiko has a reputation to manage.

183
00:10:57,394 --> 00:11:01,732
We want them to decline the match, right? So we should be doubling down.

184
00:11:02,232 --> 00:11:04,501
You're quite the lively young lady.

185
00:11:05,402 --> 00:11:07,504
She's a real free spirit, this one.

186
00:11:07,705 --> 00:11:09,940
Mommy, Reiko-san is scary.

187
00:11:10,174 --> 00:11:13,243
Remember what I told you. Turn a blind eye to any flaws.

188
00:11:13,477 --> 00:11:14,244
Flaws?!

189
00:11:14,511 --> 00:11:19,016
I got into this really great fight with some thugs the other day.

190
00:11:19,583 --> 00:11:21,752
That darn Ryo-chan...

191
00:11:24,488 --> 00:11:27,424
Oh, thanks! I was getting thirsty.

192
00:11:35,199 --> 00:11:39,103
Well, it's nice to see someone enjoying their drink. Isn't it, Kazuo-san?

193
00:11:39,336 --> 00:11:41,038
Yes... Wonderful...

194
00:11:41,372 --> 00:11:44,541
How lovely. I like your hearty demeanor.

195
00:11:44,742 --> 00:11:46,243
&lt;i&gt;Damn. You asked for this...&lt;/i&gt;

196
00:11:46,777 --> 00:11:48,879
Wow! This all looks so good!

197
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,223
Yum, yum, yummy in my tummy!

198
00:11:59,423 --> 00:12:01,725
-I can't take it anymore! -Reiko-san, don't!

199
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,928
Man, I'm stuffed.

200
00:12:05,529 --> 00:12:08,265
What a healthy appetite. Right, Kazuo-san?

201
00:12:08,465 --> 00:12:10,634
Yes, very healthy indeed...

202
00:12:10,834 --> 00:12:13,670
And they do say health is the most important thing.

203
00:12:13,904 --> 00:12:15,839
I like you more and more.

204
00:12:17,141 --> 00:12:19,276
This is tougher than I thought.

205
00:12:19,476 --> 00:12:21,011
Time for Plan B.

206
00:12:21,245 --> 00:12:22,646
Agreed.

207
00:12:23,247 --> 00:12:26,617
Well, let's let the young ones have some alone time together.

208
00:12:26,817 --> 00:12:27,651
What?!

209
00:12:28,819 --> 00:12:30,287
Let's go, Kazuo-san.

210
00:12:30,487 --> 00:12:31,588
Mommy, I'm scared.

211
00:12:31,789 --> 00:12:33,257
Come with me, you brat.

212
00:12:34,024 --> 00:12:36,560
Okay, we'll be back soon.

213
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:38,395
Take your time.

214
00:12:38,595 --> 00:12:39,463
Mommy!

215
00:12:39,797 --> 00:12:41,265
Good luck, Kazuo-san!

216
00:12:41,465 --> 00:12:42,766
Mommy!

217
00:12:42,966 --> 00:12:45,702
We're going to have so much fun together!

218
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,022
Mommy isn't here now.

219
00:13:05,255 --> 00:13:07,257
It's just you and me.

220
00:13:12,529 --> 00:13:15,666
I thought it'd be a done deal back at the restaurant.

221
00:13:15,866 --> 00:13:20,037
Poor guy. If only he'd just decline, he wouldn't have to go through this.

222
00:13:20,270 --> 00:13:21,972
Well? Let's have some fun.

223
00:13:22,172 --> 00:13:23,073
Huh?

224
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:26,910
What? Is that me? Damn, I'm creepy, even for me.

225
00:13:27,144 --> 00:13:28,679
I don't even look human.

226
00:13:28,879 --> 00:13:30,447
Hey, look at her.

227
00:13:30,647 --> 00:13:33,450
What an ugly broad. And she walks around like that?

228
00:13:33,650 --> 00:13:35,486
Could have sworn it was a pig.

229
00:13:36,987 --> 00:13:38,355
-Wait here. -What?

230
00:13:38,555 --> 00:13:40,157
Wish it were a gorilla.

231
00:13:40,357 --> 00:13:41,458
-Huh? -Ah!

232
00:13:41,658 --> 00:13:43,327
Who you callin' ugly, ugly?

233
00:13:43,894 --> 00:13:46,763
How dare you say that to me!

234
00:13:46,997 --> 00:13:48,665
Watch your mouths, you cretins!

235
00:13:48,866 --> 00:13:50,067
Sorry, ma'am.

236
00:13:50,834 --> 00:13:53,003
-Sorry about that. -No, it's okay.

237
00:13:54,071 --> 00:13:58,308
Reiko-san, you have quite a temper.

238
00:13:59,743 --> 00:14:00,744
Do you think so?

239
00:14:01,178 --> 00:14:04,781
It just really gets to me when people say mean things.

240
00:14:06,316 --> 00:14:10,387
Oh, also, my mother gave me tickets to a classical concert.

241
00:14:10,587 --> 00:14:11,755
Classical music?

242
00:14:12,222 --> 00:14:15,926
André Heilrichten Johann Autobahn is conducting a performance

243
00:14:16,126 --> 00:14:20,931
of Humboldt Undergen's Symphony No. 348 in E minor, "Song of the Forest."

244
00:14:21,498 --> 00:14:24,134
Apparently it lasts for six hours.

245
00:14:25,102 --> 00:14:29,439
Nah, I hate classical music. Let's do it another time.

246
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:32,876
We don't exactly have the same tastes. So, now what?

247
00:14:33,076 --> 00:14:35,946
You can reject the match. I don't mind.

248
00:14:36,146 --> 00:14:37,381
Oh, really?

249
00:14:37,581 --> 00:14:41,151
Yeah, it's no skin off my back. Some things just aren't meant to be.

250
00:14:41,552 --> 00:14:44,554
-Well, if you don't mind... -Yes?

251
00:14:44,755 --> 00:14:46,823
-What you were saying... -Yes?

252
00:14:47,257 --> 00:14:47,991
Oh, excuse me.

253
00:14:48,992 --> 00:14:50,527
Hello. Oh, Mommy!

254
00:14:51,161 --> 00:14:55,899
&lt;i&gt;Kazuo-san, how's the date going?&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Remember, you must get her to marry you.&lt;/i&gt;

255
00:14:56,466 --> 00:14:59,603
Um, yeah. All right, Mommy.

256
00:15:00,804 --> 00:15:04,575
We're getting along fine. No need to worry, love.

257
00:15:04,775 --> 00:15:06,376
Hello? Hello?

258
00:15:08,111 --> 00:15:10,614
I'm so very sorry. It slipped.

259
00:15:11,715 --> 00:15:13,784
Hello? Kazuo-san?

260
00:15:14,952 --> 00:15:16,186
-So? -Yes?

261
00:15:16,587 --> 00:15:18,322
Are you gonna decline the match?

262
00:15:18,555 --> 00:15:21,391
No, no. I would never turn you down.

263
00:15:21,825 --> 00:15:23,126
Really now?

264
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:27,331
&lt;i&gt;Operation Lady Lout isn't working.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Time for something else.&lt;/i&gt;

265
00:15:27,664 --> 00:15:30,634
There's something I really want. Will you buy it for me?

266
00:15:30,834 --> 00:15:32,169
Of course I will.

267
00:15:35,205 --> 00:15:37,674
&lt;i&gt;480,000 yen?&lt;/i&gt;

268
00:15:38,875 --> 00:15:41,478
You see how lovely it is?

269
00:15:41,678 --> 00:15:42,679
This one?

270
00:15:43,013 --> 00:15:44,881
&lt;i&gt;Good, he's having second thoughts.&lt;/i&gt;

271
00:15:45,315 --> 00:15:47,985
Oh, I want it, I want it, Kazuo-san.

272
00:15:48,185 --> 00:15:50,654
Hmm. You have good taste. I'll go get it.

273
00:15:50,854 --> 00:15:52,122
Whoa, really?

274
00:15:52,589 --> 00:15:56,193
Did he misread the price? It's 480,000 yen!

275
00:15:57,027 --> 00:15:59,062
Here you go, Reiko-san.

276
00:15:59,296 --> 00:16:00,831
Oh, thank you...

277
00:16:01,698 --> 00:16:03,967
&lt;i&gt;He coughed up 480,000 yen for this thing.&lt;/i&gt;

278
00:16:04,167 --> 00:16:06,837
&lt;i&gt;Fine. Enjoy showing off while you can.&lt;/i&gt;

279
00:16:07,304 --> 00:16:09,139
I want some jewelry too.

280
00:16:09,339 --> 00:16:10,207
Jewelry?

281
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,842
Yes, I want it, I want it.

282
00:16:12,042 --> 00:16:14,044
"DOKO OKAYAMA"

283
00:16:19,683 --> 00:16:23,220
&lt;i&gt;It's just a chunk of rock.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Why would anyone want this?&lt;/i&gt;

284
00:16:23,453 --> 00:16:25,889
Choose whatever you like.

285
00:16:26,556 --> 00:16:28,992
You're really giving me free reign?

286
00:16:29,192 --> 00:16:29,893
Absolutely.

287
00:16:30,093 --> 00:16:34,898
-Um, this big one for 1.2 million yen. -Okay.

288
00:16:37,634 --> 00:16:41,905
&lt;i&gt;Damn it. Just you watch, buddy.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;I'll soon make your eyes water.&lt;/i&gt;

289
00:16:42,339 --> 00:16:46,743
Um, this red one, this green one next to it, and this big one...

290
00:16:46,943 --> 00:16:48,045
Move aside, missy.

291
00:16:48,245 --> 00:16:49,112
But ma'am!

292
00:16:49,346 --> 00:16:51,848
-I want this, this, and this. -Ma'am!

293
00:16:52,049 --> 00:16:53,650
Even if she was a gorgeous babe,

294
00:16:53,850 --> 00:16:57,587
no man would stick around if she was that greedy on a first date.

295
00:16:57,821 --> 00:16:59,689
This has got to work now.

296
00:17:02,559 --> 00:17:05,095
And I'd like it all gift wrapped.

297
00:17:05,295 --> 00:17:06,530
All of it?

298
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:08,065
Yes, all of it.

299
00:17:08,265 --> 00:17:11,835
It will cost 158 million yen all together.

300
00:17:12,035 --> 00:17:13,737
One hundred and...?

301
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:19,509
"158 MILLION YEN"

302
00:17:21,678 --> 00:17:25,949
She said it's 158 million yen...

303
00:17:26,416 --> 00:17:28,218
One hundred and...

304
00:17:31,221 --> 00:17:32,055
Um...

305
00:17:32,255 --> 00:17:32,989
Yes?

306
00:17:33,223 --> 00:17:34,691
Can I pay by check?

307
00:17:35,859 --> 00:17:38,929
Hey! How do you have so much money?

308
00:17:39,129 --> 00:17:44,701
My dad gifted me a company last year. Technically, I'm the president there.

309
00:17:44,901 --> 00:17:45,802
Oh, really?

310
00:17:48,105 --> 00:17:50,874
I may not be brave or strong,

311
00:17:51,074 --> 00:17:53,543
but I do have more money than most.

312
00:17:53,743 --> 00:17:55,946
You'll be in good hands, Reiko-san.

313
00:17:56,146 --> 00:17:59,783
&lt;i&gt;All this for a bowl of katsudon...&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Time for another approach.&lt;/i&gt;

314
00:18:02,319 --> 00:18:03,286
It didn't work.

315
00:18:03,487 --> 00:18:05,122
I don't believe it.

316
00:18:05,322 --> 00:18:07,457
Now it's our time to shine.

317
00:18:08,959 --> 00:18:11,027
Is there anything else you want?

318
00:18:11,261 --> 00:18:13,463
No, this is enough.

319
00:18:13,830 --> 00:18:15,031
What's with her?

320
00:18:15,265 --> 00:18:16,833
The guy looks like a dork too.

321
00:18:17,033 --> 00:18:19,169
It's a miracle she even has a boyfriend.

322
00:18:24,341 --> 00:18:25,308
Hey, Reiko-san.

323
00:18:25,675 --> 00:18:27,577
So handsome!

324
00:18:27,777 --> 00:18:30,013
-Oh, Kei-chan! It's you! -Huh?!

325
00:18:31,014 --> 00:18:31,815
Ryotsu!

326
00:18:32,015 --> 00:18:35,285
Just deal with it. You can have my katsudon pickles.

327
00:18:35,619 --> 00:18:37,687
Reiko-san, is this a friend?

328
00:18:37,921 --> 00:18:40,590
This is my ex. Isn't he cool?

329
00:18:40,791 --> 00:18:42,292
No way!

330
00:18:42,626 --> 00:18:45,462
Oh, Reiko-chan. How did I ever let you get away?

331
00:18:45,662 --> 00:18:50,300
Stop it, you'll make me want to play with fire again.

332
00:18:52,636 --> 00:18:54,638
Hey, Reiko-san. I miss you.

333
00:18:54,838 --> 00:18:55,872
Huh?!

334
00:18:56,206 --> 00:18:58,375
Oh no, it's my other ex, Hunky Honda.

335
00:18:58,608 --> 00:18:59,476
Your other ex?

336
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:02,812
Reiko-san, let's take my... car...

337
00:19:05,815 --> 00:19:08,418
Don't laugh. I'm doing this for you.

338
00:19:08,652 --> 00:19:09,419
But...

339
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:13,623
Would you like to come for a drive to Haneda with me?

340
00:19:13,823 --> 00:19:17,360
No, come with me for a drive to Yokohama.

341
00:19:17,561 --> 00:19:21,431
Sorry, fellas. I'm on a date right now. But we'll keep in touch.

342
00:19:22,365 --> 00:19:23,500
See you, Reiko-san.

343
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,669
I still love you, Reiko-san.

344
00:19:28,371 --> 00:19:29,506
Bye-bye!

345
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,641
I don't believe it.

346
00:19:32,442 --> 00:19:37,581
Oh dear. I'm so popular, I need multiple mes to satisfy everyone.

347
00:19:38,181 --> 00:19:39,883
&lt;i&gt;Well? Gonna throw in the towel?&lt;/i&gt;

348
00:19:41,818 --> 00:19:46,890
Well, I guess you do become a socialite when you live overseas for so long.

349
00:19:47,724 --> 00:19:50,360
I know you'll be a great company president's wife.

350
00:19:52,429 --> 00:19:56,866
I'm shy, and I don't have many friends, so I envy you, Reiko-san.

351
00:19:58,468 --> 00:20:00,136
Ah, that was painful.

352
00:20:00,370 --> 00:20:02,772
Operation Man-Eater hasn't worked.

353
00:20:03,006 --> 00:20:03,673
What?

354
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:06,409
It's time to pull out the big guns.

355
00:20:08,078 --> 00:20:09,913
Good luck, Terai.

356
00:20:10,113 --> 00:20:11,114
Yeah...

357
00:20:12,749 --> 00:20:14,718
I don't feel great about this.

358
00:20:15,151 --> 00:20:17,220
They'll be here soon.

359
00:20:17,787 --> 00:20:19,022
&lt;i&gt;Then it's go time.&lt;/i&gt;

360
00:20:19,589 --> 00:20:20,790
Hey, buddy.

361
00:20:21,024 --> 00:20:22,492
Help!

362
00:20:22,726 --> 00:20:25,495
I hate wimpy guys! Goodbye.

363
00:20:25,895 --> 00:20:28,164
&lt;i&gt;This'll create a reason to reject him.&lt;/i&gt;

364
00:20:28,798 --> 00:20:30,700
I feel sorry for the poor guy,

365
00:20:30,901 --> 00:20:34,104
but with Ryotsu doing the rejecting, we're bound to succeed.

366
00:20:34,804 --> 00:20:35,805
This way.

367
00:20:36,039 --> 00:20:37,574
Where are we going?

368
00:20:37,774 --> 00:20:39,309
Somewhere nice.

369
00:20:39,509 --> 00:20:43,446
&lt;i&gt;That's odd. Terai and the others&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;should be waiting around here.&lt;/i&gt;

370
00:20:46,149 --> 00:20:48,051
They're late.

371
00:20:48,885 --> 00:20:50,620
&lt;i&gt;Where the hell did they go?&lt;/i&gt;

372
00:20:50,987 --> 00:20:54,624
I've never walked around a place like this before.

373
00:20:54,824 --> 00:20:57,294
Hey, punk. What're you looking at?

374
00:20:57,494 --> 00:20:58,962
Finally. There's Terai...

375
00:20:59,162 --> 00:21:00,330
Huh? Uh-oh...

376
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:03,266
-Do you know who we are? -They're real gangsters.

377
00:21:03,466 --> 00:21:05,769
Reiko-san! Help me!

378
00:21:08,071 --> 00:21:10,340
Wah! I'm too scared!

379
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:13,944
&lt;i&gt;It's not what we planned,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;but I'll still be able to reject him.&lt;/i&gt;

380
00:21:15,078 --> 00:21:18,682
Asking a woman to save you? What a loser.

381
00:21:18,915 --> 00:21:19,616
Take this!

382
00:21:20,016 --> 00:21:20,750
Chump!

383
00:21:21,551 --> 00:21:22,619
Hey, bozo!

384
00:21:22,819 --> 00:21:24,354
You'd better apologize.

385
00:21:24,821 --> 00:21:26,956
Knock it off, you hooligans.

386
00:21:27,957 --> 00:21:29,192
What's with the hag?

387
00:21:29,659 --> 00:21:31,161
Shut it, ugly.

388
00:21:31,661 --> 00:21:32,529
Ugly?

389
00:21:32,929 --> 00:21:34,397
Who you callin' ugly, ugly?

390
00:21:34,631 --> 00:21:35,231
Damn you!

391
00:21:37,801 --> 00:21:39,936
Boss!

392
00:21:42,572 --> 00:21:43,473
Damn you!

393
00:22:04,427 --> 00:22:06,262
I had fun today.

394
00:22:06,496 --> 00:22:09,866
But I'm crass, a gold digger, and a flirt.

395
00:22:10,066 --> 00:22:12,202
You deserve someone better.

396
00:22:12,736 --> 00:22:15,372
You can reject the match. I don't mind.

397
00:22:15,572 --> 00:22:16,406
Reiko-san.

398
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:17,841
Yes?

399
00:22:18,708 --> 00:22:20,143
Will you marry me?

400
00:22:20,377 --> 00:22:21,077
Eh?

401
00:22:21,578 --> 00:22:23,847
You're the perfect woman for me.

402
00:22:24,047 --> 00:22:25,081
What?

403
00:22:25,281 --> 00:22:27,550
At first, I was a little scared of you.

404
00:22:27,751 --> 00:22:31,087
But you're strong and reliable. Plus you're a stylish socialite.

405
00:22:31,287 --> 00:22:33,023
You're perfect!

406
00:22:33,223 --> 00:22:35,992
I can't imagine being with anyone other than you!

407
00:22:36,192 --> 00:22:37,227
H-Hold on a minute!

408
00:22:37,427 --> 00:22:38,294
Reiko-san!

409
00:22:38,528 --> 00:22:40,630
No!

410
00:22:42,599 --> 00:22:45,602
Have you heard anything from your father?

411
00:22:46,169 --> 00:22:47,370
No, nothing.

412
00:22:47,570 --> 00:22:50,407
So the match fell through then?

413
00:22:50,607 --> 00:22:52,609
It seems like such a waste.

414
00:22:53,043 --> 00:22:54,911
But thank you for your help.

415
00:22:55,278 --> 00:22:56,946
Especially you, Ryo-chan.

416
00:22:57,180 --> 00:22:58,615
Huh? Oh, uh, yeah.

417
00:23:01,551 --> 00:23:02,619
Oh!

418
00:23:04,621 --> 00:23:05,922
Congratulations, Reiko!

419
00:23:06,122 --> 00:23:08,058
I hear you got engaged!

420
00:23:08,258 --> 00:23:09,392
What?

421
00:23:10,894 --> 00:23:12,128
Reiko-san!

422
00:23:12,462 --> 00:23:13,329
No way!

423
00:23:13,563 --> 00:23:14,631
What's going on?

424
00:23:14,864 --> 00:23:16,199
Ryotsu? Ryotsu!

425
00:23:16,599 --> 00:23:19,135
-Kazuo-san, I'm here! -Huh?

426
00:23:19,335 --> 00:23:21,404
-What? -Reiko-san!

427
00:23:21,604 --> 00:23:23,139
-Kazuo-san! -Reiko-san!

428
00:23:24,307 --> 00:23:28,912
Let's go buy you that half-scale radio controlled helicopter like I promised.

429
00:23:29,112 --> 00:23:29,979
I'm so happy!

430
00:23:30,213 --> 00:23:34,918
And I also want the BUGATTI Atlantic high-end metal kit from Italy.

431
00:23:35,118 --> 00:23:36,252
Can I have it?

432
00:23:36,453 --> 00:23:37,687
Of course!

433
00:23:38,288 --> 00:23:40,523
What the hell are you thinking?!

434
00:23:40,757 --> 00:23:43,626
How long do you expect to get away with this?!

435
00:23:43,827 --> 00:23:45,228
Whatever do you mean?

436
00:23:45,929 --> 00:23:49,899
I'm going to marry Kazuo-san and live happily ever after.

437
00:23:50,099 --> 00:23:51,267
Let's go, Kazuo-san.

438
00:23:51,468 --> 00:23:52,535
Okay, Reiko-san.

439
00:23:52,769 --> 00:23:55,171
I also have a list of other things I want.

440
00:23:55,371 --> 00:23:57,774
-For you? Anything. -I'm so happy!

441
00:23:58,608 --> 00:24:01,644
You moron!

442
00:24:02,912 --> 00:24:08,785
HONDARA FIST IN CANADA!
